Package: MissingMediatorAnalysis
Type: Package
Title: Mediation Analysis with a Partially Missing Mediator and Outcome
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Haoyu", "Yang", email = "haoyuyang@hsph.harvard.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Product-of-coefficients mediation analysis when the mediator,
    and optionally the outcome, are partially missing at random given fully
    observed synthetic surrogates. Sequential synthetic surrogate (SynSurr)
    analysis estimates both paths from three least-squares fits that use all
    subjects through the surrogates. Alternatives for the mediator-outcome
    path include the efficient augmented inverse probability weighted (AIPW)
    estimator of Qin, Zhang and Leung (2017) and its combination with
    complete-case regression. Inference on the indirect effect uses the
    stacked influence functions of both paths, so the cross-path covariance
    is accounted for.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: stats, utils, parallel, splines
